---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site, operator } from "../site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who publishes Creator Growth Tools, what it covers, and how it is funded.">
  <section class="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>A small, deliberately narrow review site.</h1>
    <p class="dek">
      {site.name} publishes comparisons of the software creators and one-person businesses actually
      pay for. It is written for someone mid-decision who wants the trade-offs stated plainly and
      the sources shown.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who publishes it</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is published by <a href={operator.url} rel="noopener">{operator.name}</a>, an
        independent one-person studio based in {operator.location} that builds small AI and
        automation tooling. There is no editorial team. Reaching the person
        who writes these pages takes one email: <a href={`mailto:${operator.email}`}>{operator.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
      <p>
        We separate verified vendor facts from editorial assessment, and every article states which
        it is built on using a visible evidence grade. If we have not used a product first-hand, we
        do not claim hands-on testing or personal experience. See
        <a href="/how-we-test/">how we review</a> for what each grade requires.
      </p>

      <h2>Current scope</h2>
      <p>
        We cover newsletter and email platforms and AI voice tools for creators and one-person
        businesses. <a href="/topics/">Topics</a> lists every category we publish in. We add a
        category only when we can keep its guides verified, and would rather run a small library
        we can maintain than a catalog we cannot.
      </p>

      <h2>How this site is funded</h2>
      <p>
        Some outbound links are affiliate links, and every product button is labeled on the page so
        you can see which is which before you click. Vendor names in the body of an article link to
        the vendor's own site and are never referral links. Links that are not affiliate links earn us nothing, and
        a page with no affiliate link says exactly that. Affiliate relationships never decide which
        tool we recommend; see our <a href="/editorial-methodology/">editorial policy</a> and
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">how we make money</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How AI is used here</h2>
      <p>
        {operator.name} builds AI tooling, and AI assists the production of these pages — drafting,
        structuring, and checking consistency. It is not used to invent experience, sources, prices,
        screenshots, or results. Material product facts are checked against official vendor sources.
        Patterns from verified public reviews and community discussions are identified separately,
        and estimates are labeled as estimates. Each article's evidence grade describes the basis
        for its claims.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
